-- Interpretation --------------------------------------------
   Deterministic relations through round 3 are unavoidable in any
   Feistel network: after r rounds one output half equals a known
   function of the inputs. An impossible differential is only
   interesting if it survives past full diffusion (round 4 here).
   Key recovery on top of an r-round impossible differential
   typically covers r + 3 to r + 4 rounds.

